+++ b/skills/presentation/SKILL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,147 @@
+---
+name: presentation
+description: Creates or modifies a browser presentation modeled as one evolving diagrammatic scene (stable entities that appear, move, connect and re-label across named steps). Use when asked to make, build, edit, or extend a presentation, talk, or slide-style explainer from a topic.
+---
+
+# Presentation
+
+Build a browser presentation as **one scene that evolves through named steps**, not a deck of
+unrelated slides. Entities keep a stable identity from step to step and animate in place.
+"Presentation" is the canonical term; "talk" is an informal synonym (the entry component is
+still called `Talk.tsx`).
+
+Paths below are relative to **this file's directory** (`<skill>`), which holds
+`scripts/scaffold.mjs` and `templates/`. Always resolve templates from there, never from the
+current working directory.
+
+## 1. Gather requirements
+
+Ask the user clarifying questions **one at a time**, in this order, and wait for each answer:
+
+1. the topic,
+2. the visual style (palette, typography, mood),
+3. the content and visual description of each step (what appears, moves, connects, or changes).
+
+Do not assume details the user can still supply. Skip a question only when the prompt already
+answers it. If the prompt already contains the topic, the style, and every step, build
+without further questions.
+
+The user decides how much to specify. When they explicitly choose to build with partial
+detail, build from what you captured and offer to iterate; there is no completeness gate. Do
+not treat an unanswered question as consent to proceed.
+
+For a key or complex step you MAY draw an ASCII mockup to confirm the layout. It is optional
+and not needed for every step.
+
+## 2. Resolve the target and scaffold what is missing
+
+Run `node <skill>/scripts/scaffold.mjs detect <project root>`. It reports the target
+directory, why it was chosen, which of the three **contract anchors** exist there, and whether
+confirmation is needed:
+
+1. **Build setup**: a Vite + React + TypeScript app whose `npm run build` works.
+2. **Scene kit**: the presentation-agnostic engine (`Step`/`Scene` contract, stage host,
+   present/browse navigation, chrome, fit-scaled canvas).
+3. **Presentation index**: the registry mapping each presentation to its own route.
+
+Detection is by contract, not by byte-identical files, so renamed files or extra dependencies
+do not trigger re-scaffolding.
+
+Target rules:
+
+- Empty or standalone (non-monorepo) project: the app lives at the repository root.
+- Monorepo (`workspaces` in `package.json`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, or a `packages/` or
+  `apps/` directory): scaffold a self-contained app in `presentations/`. Never modify the
+  monorepo root, and never count the root's build as satisfying the app's anchors.
+- An existing presentation app (kit or index already present, at the root or in
+  `presentations/`) is reused as the target.
+
+Then:
+
+- All three anchors present: skip scaffolding and go to step 3.
+- In a **non-empty project where any anchor is missing** (including only the build setup),
+  state the target directory and the reason, and proceed **only after the user confirms**.
+  An empty directory needs no confirmation.
+- Otherwise run `node <skill>/scripts/scaffold.mjs apply <target> --install`. It copies only
+  the files of missing anchors, never overwrites an existing file, merges the missing
+  dependencies into `package.json`, then runs `npm install` and installs Playwright's
+  Chromium. Never assume dependencies are already installed. If it lists skipped files (for
+  example an existing `src/main.tsx`), wire them to the router yourself.
+  If it reports `incompatible` dependencies (an existing major version that differs from what
+  the kit needs, for example React 18 against React 19), tell the user and ask before
+  upgrading them; do not report the scaffold as working until the build passes.
+
+The scaffold is styling-framework-neutral: no Tailwind, theme, colors, fonts, or card/button
+styles. Add a styling framework only if the host project already uses one or the user asks.
+
+## 3. Create or modify
+
+### Create
+
+Run `node <skill>/scripts/scaffold.mjs new <target> <slug> "<Title>"`. It writes
+`src/presentations/<slug>/` (`entities.ts`, `Scene.tsx`, `steps.ts`, `Talk.tsx`, `talk.css`)
+and appends one line to `src/presentations/index.ts`, leaving every other presentation
+untouched. Then replace the placeholder content:
+
+- `entities.ts`: this presentation's `layoutId` namespace, introduction step and geometry.
+- `Scene.tsx` / `steps.ts`: steps sharing a `groupKey` and `Scene` keep one mounted scene and
+  only the payload changes. Keep continuing entities mounted with the same id so they morph
+  in place; wrap only newcomers in `Appear` (it enters after layout settles) and wrap
+  conditionally rendered entities in `AnimatePresence` so departing ones animate out.
+- Each step needs a stable `id`, an `era` label, a one-line `title`, and a paragraph `caption`.
+- The canvas is 880 x 380; place entities with literal coordinates (`at`) or presentation CSS.
+  Preserve intentional overlaps and stacks rather than spreading entities apart.
+
+**Styling belongs to the presentation.** Put the look in `talk.css` (plain CSS by default) or
+the host app, targeting the kit's `data-presentation-*` hooks. Never add colors, fonts,
+borders, shadows, or theme tokens to `src/presentation-kit/`. In `talk.css`, make the active
+progress dot and table-of-contents entry (`[data-presentation-active]`) visibly distinct and
+style the attribution (`[data-presentation-attribution]`) so it is legible.
+
+### Modify
+
+If the target presentation is unspecified or ambiguous, **list the existing presentations
+and ask which one before changing anything**. Once identified, ask only about the requested
+changes (steps, entities, or style) and edit that presentation (plus its registry line if
+needed). Do not re-run the full create flow.
+
+## 4. Self-verify before reporting done
+
+Do not report success until all of these pass; when one fails, fix it and re-check.
+
+1. `npm run build` completes with no type errors.
+2. The presentation you created or modified renders every step with no runtime or console
+   errors: run `npm run verify -- <slug>` (full build plus every step of that route) before
+   completion; a quicker build plus single-route check is fine while iterating. Plain
+   `npm run verify` checks only the default route, which is not enough.
+3. Visual composition: run `npm run inspect -- <slug>`, the project-local screenshot helper
+   (screenshots land in `.presentation-inspect/<slug>/`, taken after animations settle). If it
+   is unavailable, write any temporary Playwright helper under the project root so it
+   resolves local dependencies, never outside the tree. Inspect the first step, the last
+   step, and every dense or key step, plus a narrow viewport (`--viewport 480x800`) when the
+   presentation is responsive-sensitive. Important content must fit the canvas, intentional
+   overlaps must stay readable, and nothing may collide with the caption, progress dots,
+   table of contents, or navigation controls.
+4. Review each advisory warning the helper prints, including console or page errors it saw while stepping. Fix accidental overlaps, indistinct
+   current-step chrome, and unpolished attribution. Mark a genuinely intentional, readable
+   overlap by putting `data-presentation-allow-overlap` on the smallest subtree containing
+   both elements, and only there. Re-run the helper afterwards.
+
+## Quality bar
+
+Every presentation builds without type errors, renders its first step without runtime errors,
+shows a caption for every step, supports next/previous navigation, conforms to the
+evolving-scene model (stable entities morph, newcomers enter after others settle), and passes
+the visual composition check above.
+
+## Kit hooks
+
+Stable hooks for presentation CSS: `data-presentation-root`, `-mode`, `-header`, `-marker`,
+`-era`, `-step-number`, `-brand-slot`, `-stage`, `-canvas`, `-node` (box, label, arrow, chip,
+frame, emphasis), `-id`, `-footer`, `-title`, `-caption`, `-controls`, `-prev`, `-next`,
+`-progress`, `-progress-item`, `-toc`, `-toc-entry`, `-attribution`, and `-active` on the
+current progress item or table-of-contents entry (which also carries `aria-current`). The
+root exposes `data-step-count` and zero-based `data-step-index`. Keys: Right/Space/PageDown
+next, Left/PageUp back, `P` toggles present and browse; navigation clamps at both ends.
+Props on `<Presentation>`: `attribution` (`false` removes it, `{ content }` replaces it),
+`brand` (host top-left brand, empty by default), `canvas` (override the 880 x 380 design size).
diff --git a/skills/presentation/scripts/scaffold.mjs b/skills/presentation/scripts/scaffold.mjs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..c05cfa4aac6e2a9b6cc991510345638e647d0751
--- /dev/null
+++ b/skills/presentation/scripts/scaffold.mjs
@@ -0,0 +1,237 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env node
+// Helper for the presentation skill: detect scaffold anchors, resolve where the
+// presentation app belongs, scaffold what is missing, and add a presentation.
+// Templates are resolved relative to this file, never the caller's cwd.
+//
+//   node scaffold.mjs detect <projectRoot>
+//   node scaffold.mjs apply <targetDir> [--install]
+//   node scaffold.mjs new <targetDir> <slug> <title>
+import { spawn } from 'node:child_process'
+import { cp, mkdir, readFile, readdir, stat, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises'
+import path from 'node:path'
+import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'
+
+export const SKILL_DIR = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..')
+export const BOOTSTRAP_DIR = path.join(SKILL_DIR, 'templates', 'bootstrap')
+export const PRESENTATION_DIR = path.join(SKILL_DIR, 'templates', 'presentation')
+
+const exists = (p) => stat(p).then(() => true, () => false)
+const readJson = (p) => readFile(p, 'utf8').then(JSON.parse, () => null)
+
+async function listFiles(dir, skip = new Set(['node_modules', 'dist', '.git'])) {
+  const out = []
+  for (const entry of await readdir(dir, { withFileTypes: true }).catch(() => [])) {
+    if (skip.has(entry.name)) continue
+    const full = path.join(dir, entry.name)
+    if (entry.isDirectory()) out.push(...(await listFiles(full, skip)))
+    else out.push(full)
+  }
+  return out
+}
+
+/** Contract-level detection: keyed on what the project provides, not on exact files. */
+export async function detectAnchors(dir) {
+  const pkg = await readJson(path.join(dir, 'package.json'))
+  const deps = { ...pkg?.dependencies, ...pkg?.devDependencies }
+  const build =
+    !!pkg?.scripts?.build &&
+    ['vite', 'react', 'typescript'].every((name) => name in deps) &&
+    (await exists(path.join(dir, 'tsconfig.json')))
+
+  const sources = []
+  for (const file of await listFiles(path.join(dir, 'src'))) {
+    if (/\.[cm]?[jt]sx?$/.test(file)) sources.push(await readFile(file, 'utf8'))
+  }
+  const any = (re) => sources.some((text) => re.test(text))
+  const kit =
+    any(/export\s+(?:default\s+)?(?:function|const|class)\s+Presentation\b|export\s*\{[^}]*\bPresentation\b/) &&
+    any(/export\s+(?:type|interface)\s+Step\b|export\s+(?:type\s*)?\{[^}]*\bStep\b/) &&
+    any(/AnimatePresence/) &&
+    any(/keydown/)
+  const index = any(/slug\s*:/) && any(/load\s*:/) && (await exists(path.join(dir, 'src', 'presentations')))
+  return { build, kit, index }
+}
+
+export async function isEmptyProject(dir) {
+  const entries = await readdir(dir).catch(() => [])
+  return entries.every((name) => name === '.git')
+}
+
+export async function hasMonorepoSignal(root) {
+  const pkg = await readJson(path.join(root, 'package.json'))
+  if (pkg?.workspaces) return true
+  return (
+    (await exists(path.join(root, 'pnpm-workspace.yaml'))) ||
+    (await exists(path.join(root, 'packages'))) ||
+    (await exists(path.join(root, 'apps')))
+  )
+}
+
+/**
+ * Decides where the presentation app lives. Anchors are judged in the resolved
+ * target directory; a monorepo root's own build never satisfies them.
+ */
+export async function resolveTarget(root) {
+  const empty = await isEmptyProject(root)
+  const rootAnchors = await detectAnchors(root)
+  let target = root
+  let reason = 'standalone project: scaffold at the repository root'
+  if (empty) {
+    reason = 'empty directory: scaffold at the root'
+  } else if (rootAnchors.kit || rootAnchors.index) {
+    reason = 'existing presentation app at the root'
+  } else {
+    const nested = path.join(root, 'presentations')
+    const nestedAnchors = await detectAnchors(nested)
+    if (nestedAnchors.kit || nestedAnchors.index) {
+      target = nested
+      reason = 'existing presentation app in presentations/'
+    } else if (await hasMonorepoSignal(root)) {
+      target = nested
+      reason = 'monorepo: scaffold a self-contained app in presentations/'
+    }
+  }
+  const anchors = target === root ? rootAnchors : await detectAnchors(target)
+  const missing = Object.keys(anchors).filter((name) => !anchors[name])
+  return { target, reason, empty, anchors, missing, needsConfirmation: !empty && missing.length > 0 }
+}
+
+/** Verification and inspection tooling is copied whenever anything is scaffolded, since the package scripts depend on it. */
+const isTooling = (relative) => relative.startsWith('scripts/')
+
+function groupOf(relative) {
+  if (relative.startsWith('src/presentation-kit/')) return 'kit'
+  if (
+    relative.startsWith('src/presentations/') ||
+    ['src/Router.tsx', 'src/Landing.tsx', 'src/routes.ts', 'src/main.tsx'].includes(relative)
+  ) {
+    return 'index'
+  }
+  return 'build'
+}
+
+const major = (range) => /\d+/.exec(String(range))?.[0]
+
+/**
+ * Adds missing scripts and dependencies without changing existing ones. Returns
+ * the dependencies whose existing major version differs from what the kit needs.
+ */
+async function mergePackageJson(targetFile, templateFile, targetDir) {
+  const current = await readJson(targetFile)
+  const template = await readJson(templateFile)
+  const merged = { ...current }
+  const incompatible = []
+  for (const field of ['scripts', 'dependencies', 'devDependencies']) {
+    merged[field] = { ...template[field], ...current[field] }
+  }
+  for (const field of ['dependencies', 'devDependencies']) {
+    for (const [name, required] of Object.entries(template[field])) {
+      const existing = current[field]?.[name]
+      if (existing && major(existing) !== major(required)) incompatible.push({ name, existing, required })
+    }
+  }
+  // Drop template commands whose script files were not copied; never touch the project's own scripts.
+  for (const name of Object.keys(template.scripts)) {
+    if (current.scripts?.[name] !== undefined) continue
+    const file = /node (scripts\/\S+)/.exec(merged.scripts[name])?.[1]
+    if (file && !(await exists(path.join(targetDir, file)))) delete merged.scripts[name]
+  }
+  await writeFile(targetFile, `${JSON.stringify(merged, null, 2)}\n`)
+  return incompatible
+}
+
+/** Copies only the missing anchors' files; never overwrites an existing file. */
+export async function scaffold(targetDir, anchors) {
+  const result = { copied: [], skipped: [], merged: [], incompatible: [] }
+  const missing = Object.entries(anchors).filter(([, present]) => !present).map(([name]) => name)
+  if (missing.length === 0) return result
+  await mkdir(targetDir, { recursive: true })
+  const hadPackage = await exists(path.join(targetDir, 'package.json'))
+  for (const file of await listFiles(BOOTSTRAP_DIR, new Set(['node_modules']))) {
+    const relative = path.relative(BOOTSTRAP_DIR, file).split(path.sep).join('/')
+    if (!isTooling(relative) && !missing.includes(groupOf(relative))) continue
+    if (relative === 'package.json' || relative === 'package-lock.json') continue
+    const target = path.join(targetDir, relative)
+    if (await exists(target)) {
+      result.skipped.push(relative)
+      continue
+    }
+    await mkdir(path.dirname(target), { recursive: true })
+    await cp(file, target)
+    result.copied.push(relative)
+  }
+  // Dependencies are never assumed present: add every one that is missing.
+  if (hadPackage) {
+    result.incompatible = await mergePackageJson(path.join(targetDir, 'package.json'), path.join(BOOTSTRAP_DIR, 'package.json'), targetDir)
+    result.merged.push('package.json')
+  } else {
+    for (const name of ['package.json', 'package-lock.json']) {
+      await cp(path.join(BOOTSTRAP_DIR, name), path.join(targetDir, name))
+      result.copied.push(name)
+    }
+  }
+  return result
+}
+
+function run(command, args, cwd) {
+  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
+    const child = spawn(command, args, { cwd, stdio: 'inherit' })
+    child.on('error', reject)
+    child.on('close', (code) => (code === 0 ? resolve() : reject(new Error(`${command} ${args.join(' ')} exited ${code}`))))
+  })
+}
+
+export async function installDependencies(dir) {
+  await run('npm', ['install'], dir)
+  await run('npx', ['playwright', 'install', 'chromium'], dir)
+}
+
+const SLUG = /^[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$/
+
+/** Writes a presentation folder from the template and appends its registry line. */
+export async function createPresentation(targetDir, slug, title) {
+  if (!SLUG.test(slug)) throw new Error(`slug "${slug}" must be kebab-case`)
+  const folder = path.join(targetDir, 'src', 'presentations', slug)
+  const registryFile = path.join(targetDir, 'src', 'presentations', 'index.ts')
+  if (await exists(folder)) throw new Error(`presentation "${slug}" already exists`)
+  const registry = await readFile(registryFile, 'utf8')
+  const fill = (text) => text.replaceAll('__SLUG__', slug).replaceAll('__TITLE__', title.replaceAll('\\', '\\\\').replaceAll("'", "\\'"))
+
+  await mkdir(folder, { recursive: true })
+  const files = []
+  for (const name of await readdir(PRESENTATION_DIR)) {
+    const text = fill(await readFile(path.join(PRESENTATION_DIR, name), 'utf8'))
+    if (name === 'registry-entry.txt') continue
+    await writeFile(path.join(folder, name), text)
+    files.push(name)
+  }
+  const entry = fill(await readFile(path.join(PRESENTATION_DIR, 'registry-entry.txt'), 'utf8'))
+  const close = registry.lastIndexOf('\n]')
+  if (close === -1) throw new Error('could not find the end of the PRESENTATIONS array in src/presentations/index.ts')
+  await writeFile(registryFile, `${registry.slice(0, close + 1)}${entry}${registry.slice(close + 1)}`)
+  return { folder, files }
+}
+
+async function main(argv) {
+  const [command, dir = process.cwd(), ...rest] = argv
+  const resolved = path.resolve(dir)
+  if (command === 'detect') {
+    console.log(JSON.stringify(await resolveTarget(resolved), null, 2))
+  } else if (command === 'apply') {
+    const result = await scaffold(resolved, await detectAnchors(resolved))
+    console.log(JSON.stringify(result, null, 2))
+    if (rest.includes('--install')) await installDependencies(resolved)
+  } else if (command === 'new') {
+    const [slug, ...title] = rest
+    console.log(JSON.stringify(await createPresentation(resolved, slug, title.join(' ') || slug), null, 2))
+  } else {
+    throw new Error('usage: scaffold.mjs detect <root> | apply <target> [--install] | new <target> <slug> <title>')
+  }
+}
+
+if (process.argv[1] === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)) {
+  main(process.argv.slice(2)).catch((error) => {
+    console.error(error instanceof Error ? error.message : error)
+    process.exitCode = 1
+  })
+}
